    "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >In this game, you have a unique chance to win a big prize<strong>!</strong> Your task is to go through a series of <strong>50 rooms</strong>, but each room presents a challenge. In every room, two doors will appear in front of you \u2013 one will lead you further along the path to winning, while the other could send you back.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><u><strong>Rules:</strong></u></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Each room has <strong>two doors</strong>, and only one of them is the correct one.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The correct door is randomly chosen in each room, meaning there is no pattern to help you figure out which way to go.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >If you pick the right door, you move on to the next room.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >If you pick the wrong door, you might be sent back several rooms or have to start the entire journey again.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >If you manage to pass through all <strong>50 rooms</strong>, you <strong>win!</strong></p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Luck is crucial \u2013 every choice is tense, and there's no way to know in advance which <strong>door</strong> is the right one. Will you take risks or play it safe? Can you make it all the way to the end and claim your well-deserved prize?</p>",
    "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >In this game, you have a unique chance to win a big prize<strong>!</strong> Your task is to go through a series of <strong>50 rooms</strong>, but each room presents a challenge. In every room, two doors will appear in front of you \u2013 one will lead you further along the path to winning, while the other could send you back.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><u><strong>Rules:</strong></u></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Each room has <strong>two doors</strong>, and only one of them is the correct one.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The correct door is randomly chosen in each room, meaning there is no pattern to help you figure out which way to go.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >If you pick the right door, you move on to the next room.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >If you pick the wrong door, you might be sent back several rooms or have to start the entire journey again.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >If you manage to pass through all <strong>50 rooms</strong>, you <strong>win!</strong></p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Luck is crucial \u2013 every choice is tense, and there's no way to know in advance which <strong>door</strong> is the right one. Will you take risks or play it safe? Can you make it all the way to the end and claim your well-deserved prize?</p>",
